+
+### 1.3.4 Effective Permission Model (SRS v1.1)
+
+Delegation is an explicit, time-bounded authorization grant — it is **not** role impersonation and it never changes anyone's permanent role (FR-DEL-006, BR-035). What a user can actually do at any moment is therefore:
+
+> **Effective Permission = Permanent Role Permissions + Currently Valid Delegations**
+
+"Currently valid" means the delegation's Status is Active **and** today's date falls within its Start Date/End Date range (FR-DEL-004). A delegation that has passed its End Date is automatically treated as Expired and grants nothing (FR-DEL-005), and a Revoked delegation grants nothing from the moment of revocation onward. This evaluation happens every time a permission check occurs, not only when the delegation is created — so a delegation that was valid yesterday and has expired overnight silently and correctly stops granting access without any user action.
+
+This model only ever **adds** a narrow, specific responsibility (Stock-In, Stock-Out, or approved report access) to a Staff account — it can never grant Administrator-only capability, and every action performed under a delegation is still attributed to the actual person who performed it (BR-033, BR-036, BR-039 §26.5.8).
