+# Visual Design Package — NovaTech Electronics Inventory Management System
+
+**Phase:** 3 — Visual Design
+**Based on (approved, unmodified):**
+- Phase 1 — System Requirements Specification (SRS) v1.0, amended by SRS v1.1 Delegation (`/docs`)
+- Phase 2 — Product Requirements + UX/UI Specification v1.1 (`/product-requirements`)
+
+**Status of this phase:** This package adds no functionality, no screens, no business rules, and no permission changes. It is a visual translation layer only — every color, type size, spacing value, component state, and screen layout traces back to a specific line in Phase 1 or Phase 2. Where Phase 2 (`07-Design-System.md`, `09-Design-Recommendations-and-Claude-Brief.md`) already defined a design decision, this package adopts it exactly rather than re-deciding it, and expands it into full component-state and screen-level coverage. This includes the SRS v1.1 Delegation amendment: SCR-020 (Delegation Management) is now part of the visual design baseline, per `product-requirements/11-Product-UX-v1.1-Changelog.md`.
+
+## How to read this package
+
+| File | Contents |
+|---|---|
+| `01-Visual-Design-Overview.md` | Design personality, principles, what to avoid, how this package relates to Phase 2 |
+| `02-Design-Tokens.md` | Machine-readable color, type, spacing, radius, border, shadow, and dimension tokens |
+| `03-Component-Library.md` | Every control's normal/hover/focus/pressed/disabled/error visual spec |
+| `04-Application-Shell.md` | Header, sidebar, content region, status strip — the reusable frame for all 20 screens |
+| `05-Screen-Designs.md` | Full visual design for all 20 approved screens (SCR-001–SCR-020) |
+| `06-Dialogs-and-States.md` | Confirmation/blocked-delete/validation/success dialogs; empty, error, loading, success states |
+| `07-Accessibility.md` | Keyboard, contrast, focus, color-independence, screen-reader-adjacent considerations |
+| `08-WinForms-Implementation-Guidelines.md` | Control mapping, what's realistic vs. not, anchor/dock guidance |
+| `09-Visual-Design-Traceability.md` | SRS → Product Requirement → UX Requirement → Screen → Visual Design matrix |
+| `10-Final-Visual-Design-Audit.md` | Completion checklist and final verdict |
+
+## Source-of-truth precedence
+
+If anything in this package appears to conflict with Phase 1 or Phase 2, **Phase 1 and Phase 2 win.** This package should be corrected, not the other way around. No requirement, business rule, permission, or screen defined in Phase 1/2 is altered here. Any open question is logged in `10-Final-Visual-Design-Audit.md` §"Items for Clarification" rather than resolved by silent assumption.
