+# 2. Design Tokens
+
+All values below are sourced from and consistent with `product-requirements/07-Design-System.md` §7.1–7.9, expanded with the additional component-dimension tokens needed for full screen and component coverage. Nothing here contradicts Phase 2.
+
+## 2.1 Color Tokens
+
+```json
+{
+  "color": {
+    "primary":              "#1E4B8F",
+    "primaryHover":         "#163A6E",
+    "primaryPressed":       "#122F59",
+    "secondary":            "#3B7A8F",
+    "background":           "#F4F6F8",
+    "surface":              "#FFFFFF",
+    "surfaceElevated":      "#FFFFFF",
+    "border":               "#D7DCE1",
+    "borderFocus":          "#1E4B8F",
+    "borderError":          "#C0392B",
+    "text":                 "#1F2933",
+    "textMuted":            "#6B7785",
+    "textDisabled":         "#9AA5B1",
+    "textInverse":          "#FFFFFF",
+    "success":              "#2E8B57",
+    "successTint":          "#E5F3EC",
+    "warning":              "#C77700",
+    "warningTint":          "#FBEBD9",
+    "error":                "#C0392B",
+    "errorTint":            "#FBEAE8",
+    "info":                 "#2E6E9E",
+    "infoTint":             "#E7F0F7",
+    "disabledBackground":   "#ECEEF1",
+    "disabledText":         "#9AA5B1",
+    "rowHover":             "#EAF1F8",
+    "rowSelected":          "#D6E4F5",
+    "rowSelectedAccent":    "#1E4B8F",
+    "rowZebra":             "#FAFBFC",
+    "sidebarBackground":    "#16324F",
+    "sidebarText":          "#DCE6F0",
+    "sidebarTextMuted":     "#8FA8C2",
+    "sidebarActiveBg":      "#1E4B8F",
+    "sidebarActiveAccent":  "#5B9BD5",
+    "statusStripBackground":"#EDEFF2"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+**Usage notes:**
+- Status tints (`successTint`, `warningTint`, `errorTint`) are the pill-badge background fills; the solid color is the icon/text on top of the tint (per Phase 2 §7.7).
+- `sidebarBackground` / `sidebarText` are new tokens for this phase (Phase 2 did not fix a sidebar-specific color, only that it's a "persistent left sidebar"). A dark-neutral sidebar (`#16324F`, a deep navy consistent with Primary) is chosen over a light sidebar to give the shell a clear anchor and visual separation from the light content area — this is a visual-design decision within Phase 2's palette family, not a new requirement. Documented as an assumption in `10-Final-Visual-Design-Audit.md`.
+- All color/background text pairings meet WCAG AA (4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text) — verified in `07-Accessibility.md` §7.4.
+
+## 2.2 Typography Tokens
+
+```json
+{
+  "typography": {
+    "fontFamily": "Segoe UI, Tahoma, Arial, sans-serif",
+    "appTitle":      { "size": 16, "weight": 600, "lineHeight": 22 },
+    "screenTitle":   { "size": 20, "weight": 600, "lineHeight": 26 },
+    "sectionTitle":  { "size": 15, "weight": 600, "lineHeight": 20 },
+    "body":          { "size": 12, "weight": 400, "lineHeight": 18 },
+    "label":         { "size": 11, "weight": 400, "lineHeight": 15 },
+    "button":        { "size": 12, "weight": 600, "lineHeight": 16 },
+    "tableHeader":   { "size": 11,   "weight": 600, "lineHeight": 15 },
+    "tableCell":     { "size": 11.5, "weight": 400, "lineHeight": 16 },
+    "metricNumber":  { "size": 24, "weight": 600, "lineHeight": 30 },
+    "helperText":    { "size": 11, "weight": 400, "lineHeight": 15 },
+    "errorText":     { "size": 11, "weight": 400, "lineHeight": 15 }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+`appTitle` (16px/600) is a new token for the shell's top-left application name — sized between Screen Title and Section Title since it's persistent chrome, not page content.
+
+## 2.3 Spacing Scale
+
+```json
+{ "spacing": { "xs": 4, "sm": 8, "md": 12, "lg": 16, "xl": 24, "xxl": 32 } }
+```
+
+- `sm` (8px): label-to-input gap
+- `lg` (16px): gap between fields within one group
+- `xl` (24px): gap between field groups
+- `xxl` (32px): dialog/panel edge padding
+
+## 2.4 Radius Tokens
+
+```json
+{
+  "radius": {
+    "input": 4,
+    "button": 4,
+    "card": 6,
+    "dialog": 6,
+    "badge": 10,
+    "sidebarActiveItem": 4
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Badge radius (10px, effectively a pill on a ~20px-tall badge) is the one deliberately rounded element in the system, per Phase 2 §7.7 "status rendered as a small colored pill badge."
+
+## 2.5 Border Tokens
+
+```json
+{
+  "border": {
+    "standard": "1px solid #D7DCE1",
+    "focus": "2px solid #1E4B8F",
+    "error": "2px solid #C0392B",
+    "divider": "1px solid #D7DCE1",
+    "sidebarActiveAccent": "3px solid #5B9BD5",
+    "rowSelectedAccent": "2px solid #1E4B8F"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+## 2.6 Shadow Tokens
+
+```json
+{ "shadow": { "none": "none" } }
+```
+
+**No drop shadows are used anywhere in this design.** Depth is communicated exclusively through background/border contrast (`surface` `#FFFFFF` on `background` `#F4F6F8`, plus 1px borders), per Phase 2 §7.4 and the "avoid unnecessary shadows" instruction. The single narrow exception, realistic in WinForms, is the native OS drop shadow WinForms itself renders around a modal dialog/MessageBox — that is an OS behavior, not an application style choice, and is not something the application draws.
+
+## 2.7 Component Dimension Tokens
