+# 3. Component Library
+
+Every visual state uses tokens from `02-Design-Tokens.md`. "Not applicable" states are noted explicitly rather than omitted, so implementers know they were considered.
+
+## 3.1 Buttons
+
+| Variant | Normal | Hover | Pressed | Focus | Disabled | Usage |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Primary | Fill `primary`, text `textInverse`, radius 4 | Fill `primaryHover` | Fill `primaryPressed` | 2px outline offset ring in `borderFocus` outside the button | Fill `disabledBackground`, text `disabledText`, no hover | Save, Login, Record Stock-In, Record Stock-Out, Save Adjustment, Generate, Print |
+| Secondary | Fill `surface`, text `primary`, 1px border `primary` | Fill `rowHover` | Fill `rowSelected` | 2px focus ring | Border/text in `disabledText`, fill `disabledBackground` | Cancel, Back, Clear Form |
+| Danger | Fill `error`, text `textInverse` | Darken ~12% | Darken further | 2px focus ring | Standard disabled treatment | Delete / Deactivate (confirming button only, inside dialogs) |
+| Ghost/Text | Transparent, text `primary`, no border | Text `primaryHover`, subtle `rowHover` background pad | Text `primaryPressed` | Underline + focus ring | Text `disabledText` | Clear Filters, "Mark Inactive" inline link, low-emphasis actions |
+
+- Height: `buttonHeightStandard` (32px) everywhere except Login's "Login" button, which uses `buttonHeightLarge` (40px) as the single-purpose, high-emphasis action on that screen.
+- Minimum width: 88px, auto-width beyond that with 16px horizontal padding.
+- One Primary button per screen/dialog maximum — this is enforced visually so the user's eye is never split between two competing "main" actions (consistent with 6.2's fixed Cancel-left/Save-right rule).
+- **Loading state** (Login "Signing in…", Save "Saving…"): label swaps to a busy label, button becomes non-interactive but keeps its Primary fill (not the disabled-gray treatment) so it doesn't visually read as blocked — it reads as "working."
+
+## 3.2 Text Fields (TextBox)
+
+| State | Border | Fill | Text | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Normal | `border` 1px | `surface` | `text` | Persistent label above, 8px gap |
+| Hover | `border` 1px (unchanged — WinForms TextBox has no meaningful hover) | `surface` | `text` | — |
+| Focus | `borderFocus` 2px | `surface` | `text` | Visible ring, no placeholder-only labels ever |
+| Error | `borderError` 2px | `surface` | `text` | Inline `errorText` message directly beneath, replacing helper text |
+| Disabled | `border` 1px | `disabledBackground` | `disabledText` | Used for QuantityOnHand, Username-on-Edit — always with an explanatory caption below (per Phase 2 §6.1 UPDATE) |
+
+Height 30px, radius 4px, internal padding 8px horizontal.
+
+## 3.3 Password Fields
+
+Same as Text Fields, plus:
+- Characters masked with `•`.
+- No visibility-toggle icon in MVP (not in the approved spec) — kept as a plain masked field to avoid inventing an unapproved control.
+- On Login error (ER-001), the password field is cleared per Phase 2 §5.1, and receives focus.
+
+## 3.4 Numeric Inputs
+
+Same visual treatment as Text Fields (right-aligned text, since these are quantities/prices), plus:
+- Non-numeric keystrokes are rejected at input time (live validation per Phase 2 §6.7).
+- Currency fields (Purchase Price, Selling Price, Unit Price) show 2 decimal places and are right-aligned for scan-friendly column alignment when they appear in forms mirroring grid columns.
+- Live computed previews (Stock-In "New on-hand will be: X", Adjustment "Difference: +5/−3/0") render as an `info`-colored (or `success`/`error` for the signed Adjustment difference) inline label directly beneath the field, `body` weight, updating on each keystroke — no button press required.
+
+## 3.5 ComboBoxes
+
+| State | Border | Fill | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Normal | `border` 1px | `surface` | Dropdown chevron icon, `textMuted` |
+| Focus | `borderFocus` 2px | `surface` | — |
+| Error (no selection made, required) | `borderError` 2px | `surface` | "Please make a selection." beneath |
+| Disabled | `border` 1px | `disabledBackground` | Used for Staff viewing Category/Supplier/Customer forms where all controls are read-only |
+
+Type-to-search ComboBoxes (Product selectors on Stock-In/Out/Adjustment) use the identical visual treatment — the type-ahead behavior is functional, not a separate visual style.
+
+## 3.6 DateTimePickers
+
+Same border/fill states as ComboBoxes. Calendar icon at the right edge, `textMuted`. Defaults to today's date where specified (Stock-In, Stock-Out dates). Dates beyond today are not selectable in the calendar popup where the rule applies (VAL-015-style "no future date" fields) — the disallowed dates render in `disabledText`, not simply omitted, so the user can see why they can't be picked.
+
+## 3.7 Checkboxes
+
+| State | Box | Check mark | Label |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Unchecked | 1px `border`, `surface` fill, 4px radius | — | `text` |
+| Checked | `primary` fill | `textInverse` check glyph | `text` |
+| Focus | Add 2px `borderFocus` ring around box | — | — |
+| Disabled | `disabledBackground` fill, `border` outline | `disabledText` check if checked | `disabledText` |
+
+Used for: Active status (Product/Category/Supplier/Customer/User Edit mode).
+
+## 3.8 Radio Buttons
+
+**Not used anywhere in the approved MVP screen set** — every choice in the spec is either a ComboBox selection (Category, Supplier, Role) or a Checkbox (Active). This is noted explicitly (per the request to define radio buttons "if needed") rather than silently omitted: if a future requirement introduces a genuine 2–3-way exclusive choice control, it should reuse the Checkbox's border/radius/focus treatment but as a circular 16px control with a filled `primary` dot when selected.
+
+## 3.9 DataGridView (Table)
+
+See `02-Design-Tokens.md` §2.1/2.7 and Phase 2 §6.5/§7.7 for full rationale. Full component spec:
+
+| Element | Spec |
+|---|---|
+| Header row | Fill `background` (`#F4F6F8`), text `text`, `tableHeader` type, 1px bottom border `border`, height `gridHeaderHeight` (32px) |
+| Header sort indicator | Small chevron icon appended to the active sort column's label, `primary` color |
+| Row (odd) | Fill `surface` (`#FFFFFF`) |
+| Row (even) | Fill `rowZebra` (`#FAFBFC`) — subtle zebra |
+| Row height | `gridRowHeight` (30px) — dense but not cramped, since scanning many rows fast is the core task |
+| Row hover | Fill `rowHover` (`#EAF1F8`) |
+| Row selected | Fill `rowSelected` (`#D6E4F5`) + 2px left accent bar in `primary` (`rowSelectedAccent`) |
+| Cell text | `tableCell` type, `text` color; numeric/currency columns right-aligned; text columns left-aligned; Status column center-aligned (it's a badge, not text) |
+| Status cell | Pill badge: icon + label + tint background (`successTint`/`warningTint`/`errorTint`) + solid-color icon/text, `badge` radius, `badgeHeight` (20px) — never a plain colored cell or colored row |
+| Action column | Rightmost, fixed-width, icon-only buttons (View/Edit/Delete) with tooltips, `iconInline` (16px) icons, ~8px gap between icons |
+| Empty state | Grid body replaced by a centered message + optional icon + optional action button (see `06-Dialogs-and-States.md` §6.4) |
+| Loading state | Lightweight centered "Loading…" label/spinner-equivalent replaces grid body briefly; grid never flashes an empty/no-records state during a real load |
+
+## 3.10 Tabs
+
+**Not used for primary navigation** (per Phase 2 §2.2, sidebar owns primary navigation). Reserved only for grouping fields within an oversized Add/Edit form if one ever needs it — not required by any MVP form (all MVP forms use GroupBox/Panel section headers instead, per §3.13 below). No tab visual spec is defined since no MVP screen uses one; if needed later, it should reuse the sidebar's active-item accent-bar convention adapted to a horizontal strip.
+
+## 3.11 Sidebar & Navigation Items
+
+See `04-Application-Shell.md` for the full shell spec. Per-item states:
+
+| State | Background | Text | Icon | Accent |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Normal | transparent (`sidebarBackground` shows through) | `sidebarText` | `sidebarText` | none |
+| Hover | slightly lighter navy tint (`primary` at low opacity equivalent, e.g. blend toward `#1E4B8F` at ~25%) | `sidebarText` | `sidebarText` | none |
+| Active | `sidebarActiveBg` (`#1E4B8F`) fill, full row | `textInverse` | `textInverse` | 3px left bar `sidebarActiveAccent` (`#5B9BD5`) |
+| Disabled/Hidden | Not rendered at all for role-inapplicable items (Inventory Adjustment, User Management for Staff) — see §3.11.1 | — | — | — |
+
+### 3.11.1 Hidden vs. Disabled
+
+Per Phase 2 §5.11/§3.2 (UX-DEC-001) and §3.3/§9.1a (UX-DEC-002), Inventory Adjustment, User Management, and **Delegation Management** are **entirely hidden** from Staff's sidebar, not shown-and-disabled. This is a deliberate visual decision, not an oversight: showing a permanently disabled nav item to a role that will never have access to it adds visual noise and an implied "maybe someday" that isn't true. Anywhere a control is merely *situationally* restricted (e.g., an Administrator's own "Deactivate" row on User Management), the disabled-with-tooltip treatment from §3.1 is used instead, because that restriction is state-dependent, not role-permanent. The same absent-not-disabled principle applies *inside* SCR-020 itself: non-delegatable responsibilities (User Management, Inventory Adjustment, Administrator privileges, master-data deletion/deactivation) never appear as options in the Responsibility ComboBox at all — there is no disabled option to hover or wonder about (Phase 2 BR-036, PR-020).
+
+## 3.12 Badges / Status Indicators
+
+Single component, three semantic variants, reused identically everywhere status appears (Product List, Product Details, Dashboard tiles, Stock-Out selector, Reports) per Phase 2 §6.3:
+
+| Status | Icon | Text color/icon color | Tint background | Label |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| In Stock | check-circle | `success` | `successTint` | "In Stock" |
+| Low Stock | warning-triangle | `warning` | `warningTint` | "Low Stock" |
+| Out of Stock | circle-cross | `error` | `errorTint` | "Out of Stock" |
+| Active (entity status) | check-circle (smaller/muted variant) | `success` | `successTint` | "Active" |
+| Inactive (entity status) | circle-cross (muted) | `textMuted` | `disabledBackground` | "Inactive" |
+| Active (delegation, SCR-020) | check-circle | `success` | `successTint` | "Active" |
+| Expired (delegation, SCR-020) | clock | `textMuted` | `disabledBackground` | "Expired" |
+| Revoked (delegation, SCR-020) | circle-cross | `error` | `errorTint` | "Revoked" |
+
+Shape: pill (`badge` radius), `badgeHeight` 20px, icon 14px inline-left, 6px gap to label text (11px semibold).
+
+Delegation status (per Phase 2 §6.3.1) reuses the identical component and, notably, the identical token pairs as existing statuses rather than inventing new ones — Active reuses the In-Stock/entity-Active pairing, Expired reuses the Inactive pairing (a neutral, non-alarming "this just isn't current" treatment, not an error), and Revoked reuses the Out-of-Stock/error pairing (an explicit administrative action, weighted accordingly).
+
+## 3.13 Section Headers (GroupBox/Panel-with-header)
+
+Used inside forms with more than ~6 fields (Product, User, Stock-In, Stock-Out, Adjustment), per Phase 2 §6.4:
+- Header: `sectionTitle` type (15px/600), `text` color, 1px bottom `divider` border spanning the group width, 8px padding below header before first field.
+- Group spacing: `xl` (24px) between groups; `lg` (16px) between fields within a group.
+- Short forms (Category, Supplier, Customer — ≤6 fields) skip grouping entirely and use a flat field list, per the same rule — grouping only where it earns its complexity.
+
+## 3.14 Dialogs
+
+See `06-Dialogs-and-States.md` for full content/copy patterns. Structural spec:
+- Modal, centered on parent window, `dialog` radius (6px), `surface` fill, no shadow beyond the OS-native modal shadow.
+- Title bar: `sectionTitle`/H2 type, states action + entity ("Add Product," "Delete Supplier?").
+- Body padding: `xxl` (32px).
+- Footer: Cancel (secondary, left of Save) / Save-or-confirming-action (primary or danger, right), per the fixed Phase 2 §6.2 button order.
+- Sizes: `dialogWidthSmall` (420px) for confirmations; `dialogWidthMedium` (560px) for short Add/Edit (Category/Supplier/Customer/User); `dialogWidthLarge` (680px) for grouped Add/Edit (Product).
+
+## 3.15 Validation Messages
+
+`errorText` type (11px), `error` color, positioned directly beneath the offending field (replacing any helper text in that space), preceded by a small inline error icon (12px). Never presented as a MessageBox for field-level issues (Phase 2 §6.7) — MessageBox is reserved for whole-form/system-level failures.
+
+## 3.16 Notification / Success Messages
+
+Transient status banner, anchored in the StatusStrip (bottom of main window) or as a slim banner directly under the header on the relevant screen: `successTint` background, `success` icon + text, auto-dismisses after ~4 seconds, non-blocking (per Phase 2 §6.9).
+
+## 3.17 Empty States
+
+See `06-Dialogs-and-States.md` §6.4 for full per-screen copy (sourced verbatim from Phase 2 §6.8). Visual pattern: centered within the grid/content area, `textMuted` icon (24–32px, outline style, no illustration), `body` message text, optional Primary or Ghost action button below.
+
+## 3.18 Search Bars
+
+TextBox visual treatment (§3.2) with a leading search icon (16px, `textMuted`) inset at the left, placeholder text in `textMuted` ("Search by name or ID…" etc., per Phase 2 §5.3). Live-filters the grid with a ~300ms debounce; no separate "Search" button.
+
+## 3.19 Filters
+
+ComboBoxes (§3.5) and DateTimePicker pairs (§3.6) laid out in a single horizontal filter bar directly above the grid, `md` (12px) gaps between controls. "Clear Filters" (Ghost button, §3.1) appears only once a filter or search term is active, right-aligned in the same bar.
+
+## 3.20 Toolbars
+
+The list-screen header itself functions as the toolbar: screen title (left) + "+ Add {Entity}" Primary button (right, Administrator only). No separate floating toolbar component is introduced — this keeps the pattern identical to the header spec in `04-Application-Shell.md` rather than adding a second, competing chrome element.
+
+## 3.21 Cards
+
+Used only for: Dashboard metric tiles and the Reports Hub report-type picker. Spec: `surface` fill, 1px `border`, `card` radius (6px), no shadow, `lg` (16px) internal padding. Not used as a general list/content pattern (grids are used for records, per §3.9) — keeps the visual vocabulary from fragmenting into "sometimes cards, sometimes tables" for the same kind of data.
+
+## 3.22 Headers (Screen Header)
+
+Every screen's header follows one pattern: `screenTitle` (20px/600) at left, primary action button (if any) at right, optional breadcrumb-style subtitle beneath the title in `label`/`textMuted` style (e.g., "Products › Edit Product"), `xl` (24px) bottom margin before content begins.
