+# 4. Main Application Shell
+
+Source: Phase 2 §2.2 (Navigation Model), §2.3 (Desktop Window Strategy), §10 (navigation style), §2.1/§9.1a (SRS v1.1 Delegation navigation). This is the single reusable frame every post-login screen (SCR-002 through SCR-020) renders inside.
+
+## 4.1 Layout Regions
+
+```
+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│  HEADER  (56px)   Screen Title / breadcrumb        [Global Search]  │
+├───────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
+│               │                                                     │
+│   SIDEBAR     │                                                     │
+│   (220px      │              CONTENT REGION                        │
+│    fixed)     │              (fills remaining space)                │
+│               │                                                     │
+│  [Dashboard]  │                                                     │
+│  ─ Catalog ─  │                                                     │
+│  [Products]   │                                                     │
+│  [Categories] │                                                     │
+│  [Suppliers]  │                                                     │
+│  [Customers]  │                                                     │
+│  ─ Inventory ─│                                                     │
+│  [Stock In]   │                                                     │
+│  [Stock Out]  │                                                     │
+│  [Adjustment] │                                                     │
+│  [History]    │                                                     │
+│  [Reports]    │                                                     │
+│               │                                                     │
+│  ─ Admin ──── │                                                     │
+│  [Users]      │                                                     │
+│  [Delegation] │                                                     │
+│               │                                                     │
+│  [Logout]     │                                                     │
+├───────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
+│  STATUS STRIP (28px)  User: J. Alvarez · Role: Administrator · Today │
+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+
+## 4.2 Header (top, 56px, `headerHeight`)
+
+- **Left:** current screen title (`screenTitle`, 20px/600, `text` color); on Add/Edit or Details screens, a breadcrumb-style subtitle beneath in `label`/`textMuted` (e.g., "Products › Edit Product").
+- **Right:** Global product-search box (per Phase 2 §2.2 header spec) — same TextBox visual treatment as §3.2/§3.18, ~280px wide, search icon inset, placeholder "Search products…". Present on every screen (not just Product List) since it's global quick-search.
+- **Background:** `surface` (`#FFFFFF`), 1px bottom `divider` border separating it from the content region.
+
+## 4.3 Sidebar (left, 220px fixed, `sidebarWidth`)
+
+- **Background:** `sidebarBackground` (`#16324F`, deep navy — see `02-Design-Tokens.md` §2.1 rationale note).
+- **App identity area (top):** application name/short logotype ("NovaTech Inventory"), `appTitle` type (16px/600), `textInverse`-equivalent (`sidebarText`), 56px tall band matching the header height so the two align across the sidebar/header seam.
+- **Navigation items:** grouped exactly per Phase 2 §2.1 IA table:
+  - **Dashboard** (ungrouped, top)
+  - **Catalog** group label (`label`, `sidebarTextMuted`, 8px top padding) → Products, Categories, Suppliers, Customers
+  - **Inventory Operations** group label → Stock In, Stock Out, Inventory Adjustment *(Admin only)*, Inventory History
+  - **Reports** (ungrouped)
+  - **User Management** and **Delegation Management** *(both Admin only, visually separated at the bottom with a divider and grouped together — Phase 2 §2.1 "bottom, Administrator-only," updated by SRS v1.1)*
+- **Item anatomy:** `iconSidebar` (24px) icon + label (`body`, 12px), 8px gap, full-row click target, `md`–`lg` (12–16px) vertical padding.
+- **States:** see `03-Component-Library.md` §3.11.
+- **Logout:** fixed at the sidebar footer, Ghost-style treatment on the dark background (icon + "Logout" label in `sidebarTextMuted`, `sidebarText` on hover). Confirms first if unsaved changes exist on an open form (Phase 2 §2.2).
+
+## 4.4 Content Region
+
+- **Background:** `background` (`#F4F6F8`).
+- **Padding:** `xl` (24px) on all sides.
+- List screens use the full available width; Add/Edit forms open as centered modal dialogs on top of this region (the underlying list stays visible behind the dialog, per Phase 2 §2.2 "context isn't lost").
+- Resizing: content region and its DataGridViews Dock/Anchor to fill remaining space as the main window resizes; sidebar width never changes (Phase 2 §2.3/§2.4).
+
+## 4.5 Status Strip (bottom, 28px, `statusStripHeight`)
+
+- **Background:** `statusStripBackground` (`#EDEFF2`), 1px top `divider` border.
+- **Left:** logged-in user's full name + role ("J. Alvarez · Administrator").
+- **Center-right:** current date.
+- **Transient area:** success/warning/error status messages appear here (per Phase 2 §6.9), replacing the date temporarily, then reverting after ~4 seconds — or appearing alongside it if space allows at typical desktop widths.
+- Type: `label`/`helperText` (11px), `textMuted` for static content, semantic color for transient messages.
+
+## 4.6 Role-Based Shell Behavior
+
+- Sidebar items for Inventory Adjustment, User Management, and Delegation Management render **only** when the logged-in user's role is Administrator (hidden, not disabled — §3.11.1).
+- Everything else in the shell (header, search, status strip, remaining nav items) is identical for both roles — role differences live in navigation *content* and screen-level *controls*, never in the shell's structure or style.
+- **Delegation is invisible as a concept in the shell, not just the sidebar (UX-DEC-002):** a Staff user with an active delegation sees no "Delegated" badge, banner, or shell indicator anywhere. The shell is rebuilt at login (and re-evaluated as delegations start/expire) purely by checking effective permission (Phase 2 §1.3.4) against the same visibility rules already used for permanent role — Stock-In/Stock-Out simply become reachable if they weren't already, with no additional shell chrome.
+
+## 4.7 Window Behavior
+
+Per Phase 2 §2.3: main window resizable/maximizable, opens maximized on 1366×768+ displays, minimum 1024×768 (`minWindowWidth`/`minWindowHeight`). Sidebar fixed-width at all sizes; content region and grids anchor/dock to fill remaining space. No mobile breakpoints.
