+# 5. Screen Designs — All 19 Approved Screens
+
+Every screen below renders inside the shell defined in `04-Application-Shell.md` (except Login, which is pre-auth and has no shell) and uses only components from `03-Component-Library.md`. Format per the audit checklist: Purpose · Layout · Hierarchy · Components · Placement · Primary Action · Secondary Actions · Data Presentation · Empty · Error · Success · Permission Differences · Resizing.
+
+List/Add-Edit screens that share the reference pattern (Category, Supplier, Customer) are documented against the pattern with only their deltas, exactly as Phase 2 §5.6–5.8 does — this keeps the design system visibly one system, not 19 unrelated screens.
+
+---
+
+## 5.1 SCR-001 — Login
+
+**Purpose:** Authenticate and load role.
+**Layout:**
+```
+┌───────────────────────────────────┐
+│           (background)             │
+│      ┌───────────────────┐         │
+│      │   NovaTech         │         │
+│      │   Inventory        │  ← appTitle, centered
+│      │  ─────────────     │
+│      │  Username           │
+│      │  [_______________]  │
+│      │  Password           │
+│      │  [_______________]  │
+│      │                     │
+│      │  [   Login   ]  ←Primary, 40px
+│      │                     │
+│      │  (inline error area)│
+│      └───────────────────┘         │
+│                    v1.0 (bottom-right)│
+└───────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+Centered card, `dialogWidthSmall` (420px), `card` radius, `surface` fill, on a plain `background` field — no sidebar, no header (nothing to navigate to pre-auth), per Phase 2 §5.1.
+
+**Visual Hierarchy:** App identity (largest, top) → fields (equal weight) → Login button (only Primary element, high-contrast, `buttonHeightLarge`) → error area (only visible on failure) → version label (smallest, `helperText`, unobtrusive corner).
+
+**Components:** Username TextBox (required), Password field (masked, required), Login button (Primary, full card width), inline error message area (hidden by default), optional version label.
+
+**Primary Action:** Login (click or Enter in Password field).
+**Secondary Actions:** None — single-purpose screen by design.
+**Data Presentation:** N/A (no data display, input only).
+**Empty State:** Default/Normal state *is* the empty state — both fields blank, focus on Username, Login disabled until both fields have content (§3.1 disabled treatment).
+**Error State:** ER-001 message in the inline error area (`errorTint` background, `error` text/icon), Password field cleared and refocused, per Phase 2 §5.1.
+**Success State:** Brief "Signing in…" busy state on the Login button (§3.1 loading treatment), then navigation to Dashboard — no persistent success message needed since the screen transition itself is the confirmation.
+**Permission Differences:** None — identical for all users pre-auth.
+**Resizing:** Card stays fixed-size and centered regardless of window size; background fills remaining space. Window is not resizable from this screen in most WinForms login-form implementations, though this design does not require that constraint.
+
+---
+
+## 5.2 SCR-002 — Dashboard
+
+**Purpose:** Orientation hub — metrics, recent activity, quick navigation.
+**Layout:**
+```
+Header: "Dashboard"                                    [search]
+┌─────────┬─────────┬─────────┬─────────┬─────────┬─────────┐
+│ Products│Categories│Suppliers│ Total Qty│Low Stock│Out of  │  ← metric tiles (cards)
+│   142   │    12    │    8    │  3,204   │    ⚠ 6  │Stock ✕2│
+└─────────┴─────────┴─────────┴─────────┴─────────┴─────────┘
+┌───────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────┐
+│ Recent Activity                │ Quick Actions              │
+│ (list: date/type/product/qty/  │ [ Record Stock-In ]        │
+│  user, read-only)              │ [ Record Stock-Out ]       │
+│                                 │ [ Search Products ]        │
+│                                 │ (Admin only, if role fits: │
+│                                 │  Inventory Adjustment,     │
+│                                 │  User Management)          │
+└───────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────┘
+```
+**Visual Hierarchy:** Metric tiles (top, scannable at a glance) → Recent Activity (left, wider — the "what's been happening" narrative) → Quick Actions (right, narrower — the "what to do next" panel, using large obvious Primary/Secondary buttons per Phase 2 §5.2/§10).
+
+**Components:** 6 metric tile Cards (§3.21: Total Active Products, Total Categories, Total Suppliers, Total Current Inventory Quantity, Low-Stock Count, Out-of-Stock Count — Low/Out tiles carry the status badge treatment, icon+label+color, §3.12), Recent Activity list/grid (§3.9, read-only, no action column), Quick Actions panel (button stack).
+
+**Primary Action:** None single-fixed — this is a hub screen; the two operationally primary actions (Record Stock-In / Stock-Out) are visually emphasized as Primary-style buttons in Quick Actions.
+**Secondary Actions:** Click a metric tile → navigates to the relevant filtered list (e.g., Low-Stock tile → Product List pre-filtered); click a Recent Activity row → Inventory History filtered to that date (Phase 2 §5.2).
+**Data Presentation:** Tiles = large `metricNumber` (24px/600) + `label` caption. Recent Activity = compact list/grid, most-recent-first.
+**Empty State:** New installation, zero products: tiles show "0", Recent Activity shows "No recent activity yet — record your first Stock-In to get started." with a direct button into Stock-In (Phase 2 §5.2, §6.8).
+**Error State:** Metrics unavailable (ER-007 class) → tile area shows "Unable to load dashboard data," rest of shell/app remains usable (Phase 2 §5.2).
+**Success State:** N/A directly on this screen (it reflects the results of actions taken elsewhere); a transient status message can still surface here if the user just completed an action and was redirected.
+**Permission Differences:** Same metric set and layout for both roles (Phase 2 §5.2 — SRS does not define a reduced metric set for Staff). Quick Actions panel omits Inventory Adjustment / User Management buttons for Staff, matching sidebar visibility.
+**Resizing:** Metric tile row wraps or compresses tile width proportionally above minimum window width; two-column lower region keeps its ratio (Recent Activity wider) down to 1024px minimum, at which point Quick Actions may stack beneath Recent Activity rather than beside it if needed to preserve grid readability.
+
+---
+
+## 5.3 SCR-003 — Product List *(reference pattern — see 5.6/5.7/5.8 for Category/Supplier/Customer deltas)*
+
+**Purpose:** Browse, search, filter products.
+**Layout:**
+```
+Header: "Products"                          [+ Add Product]  ← Admin only
+┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│ [🔍 Search by name or ID…] [Category ▾] [Supplier ▾] [Status ▾]  Clear Filters │
+├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
+│ ID  Name          Category  Supplier  Qty  Min  Status        Price   Actions │
+│ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────│
+│ 001 USB-C Cable    Cables    ACME      42   10  ● In Stock     $9.99  👁 ✏ 🗑 │
+│ 002 Wireless Mouse  Peripherals TechCo   3   10  ▲ Low Stock   $24.99 👁 ✏ 🗑 │
+│ 003 HDMI Adapter    Cables    ACME       0   5   ✕ Out of Stock $14.99 👁 ✏ 🗑 │
+├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
+│ 142 products                                              │
+└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+**Visual Hierarchy:** "+ Add Product" (Primary, top-right, most emphasized action for Admin) → search/filter bar (immediately actionable) → grid (main content, majority of screen) → row count (least emphasis, footer).
+
+**Components:** Search TextBox (§3.18), Category/Supplier/Stock-Status filter ComboBoxes (§3.19), Clear Filters ghost link (appears only when active), DataGridView (§3.9) with columns: Product ID (fixed), Name (fill/widest), Category (fixed), Default Supplier (fixed), Qty on Hand (fixed, right-aligned), Min Level (fixed, right-aligned), Status (fixed, badge), Selling Price (fixed, right-aligned currency), Actions (fixed, rightmost).
+
+**Primary Action:** "+ Add Product" (Administrator only).
+**Secondary Actions:** View (all roles), Edit/Delete (Administrator only), Search/Filter (all roles, live-updating).
+**Data Presentation:** One row per product; Status as pill badge (§3.12) — never plain colored text or a colored row, per Phase 2 §6.3.
+**Empty State (no products):** "No products yet. Add your first product to get started." + Add button (Admin) (§3.17).
+**Empty State (no matches):** "No products match your search or filters." + Clear Filters.
+**Error State:** ER-007/010-class friendly message with retry, grid body replaced.
+**Success State:** Transient status banner after an Add/Edit/Delete completes elsewhere and returns here ("Product saved successfully"), grid refreshes and the affected row briefly highlights.
+**Permission Differences:** Administrator sees "+ Add Product" and Edit/Delete action icons; Staff see the identical grid and filters but the Actions column shows View only, and "+ Add Product" is not rendered at all (not disabled — removed).
+**Resizing:** Name column fill-weighted; ID/Qty/Min/Status/Price/Actions fixed-width; grid scrolls vertically past visible rows (no pagination, per Phase 2 §6.5).
+
+---
+
+## 5.4 SCR-004 — Product Details
+
+**Purpose:** Full read-only view of one product, including calculated status.
+**Layout:**
+```
+Header: "USB-C Cable"                    ● In Stock badge (top-right of header)
+┌───────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┐
+│ Identity                   │ Stock                         │
+│ Name: USB-C Cable          │ Qty on Hand: 42                │
+│ Category: Cables           │ Minimum Level: 10               │
+│ Default Supplier: ACME     │ Status: ● In Stock (badge)      │
+│ Description: ...           │                                 │
+│ Purchase Price: $4.50      │                                 │
+│ Selling Price: $9.99       │                                 │
+├───────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┤
+│                                    [Back] [Edit] [Delete]   │ ← Admin sees Edit/Delete
+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+**Visual Hierarchy:** Product name + status badge (header, highest emphasis) → two-column read-only field area → action row (bottom, Back always leftmost/secondary style, Edit Primary for Admin, Delete/Deactivate Danger-adjacent Ghost for Admin).
+
+**Components:** Read-only labeled fields (Name, Category, Default Supplier, Description, Purchase Price, Selling Price, Quantity on Hand, Minimum Stock Level, Active/Inactive, created/modified metadata where available), Status badge in header, Back/Edit/Delete buttons.
+
+**Primary Action:** Edit (Administrator only).
+**Secondary Actions:** Delete/Deactivate (Administrator only), Back (all roles).
+**Data Presentation:** Static labeled key-value pairs, no editable controls anywhere on this screen (pure detail view, per Phase 2 §5.4) — this absence of any input styling is itself the visual signal that the screen is read-only.
+**Empty State:** N/A (always shows one specific product).
+**Error State:** Not Found (ER-008) — "The selected record no longer exists," with a Back action, replacing the field area (covers the case where the product was deleted elsewhere between list and detail load).
+**Success State:** N/A directly (edits happen on SCR-005); a transient banner can surface here on return from a successful Edit.
+**Permission Differences:** Staff see identical read-only fields and status badge but no Edit/Delete/Deactivate buttons — only Back.
+**Inactive Treatment:** Header uses a muted/greyed treatment and an "Inactive" badge (§3.12) in place of the stock-status badge when the product is inactive.
+**Resizing:** Two-column field area may collapse to one column below a width threshold if ever needed, though 1024px minimum comfortably fits two columns.
+
+---
+
+## 5.5 SCR-005 — Product Add/Edit *(reference pattern for all master-data Add/Edit dialogs)*
+
+**Purpose:** Create/update product master data.
+**Layout:** Modal dialog, `dialogWidthLarge` (680px), grouped sections (§3.13):
+```
+┌─ Add Product ───────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│ Identity                                                  │
+│  Product Name *  [_______________________]                │
+│  Description     [_______________________] (0/500)         │
+│                                                             │
+│ Category & Supplier                                        │
+│  Category *      [ ▾ Select category ]                     │
+│  Default Supplier * [ ▾ Select supplier ]                   │
+│                                                             │
+│ Pricing                                                     │
+│  Purchase Price * [____] Selling Price * [____]              │
+│                                                             │
+│ Stock Settings                                              │
+│  Minimum Stock Level * [____]                                │
+│  Quantity on Hand  [ 0 (starts at zero) ]  (disabled)         │
+│    Adjust stock using Stock-In, Stock-Out, or Adjustment.    │
+│  ☐ Active   (Edit mode only)                                 │
+│                                                             │
+│                                        [Cancel]  [Save]     │
+└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+**Visual Hierarchy:** Dialog title states action+entity → grouped fields in logical reading order (Identity → Category/Supplier → Pricing → Stock Settings) → Cancel/Save footer, fixed bottom-right per Phase 2 §6.2.
+
+**Components:** Product Name (required TextBox, red asterisk, max 100), Category (required ComboBox, active categories only), Default Supplier (required ComboBox, active suppliers only), Description (optional multiline, max 500, char counter), Purchase/Selling Price (required numeric, ≥0, 2 decimals), Minimum Stock Level (required numeric integer ≥0), Quantity on Hand (disabled/read-only with caption), Active checkbox (Edit mode only), inline validation areas per field.
+
+**Primary Action:** Save.
+**Secondary Actions:** Cancel (discards; confirms only if dirty).
+**Data Presentation:** N/A (input form); Quantity on Hand shown disabled rather than hidden, per Phase 2 §6.1 UPDATE rationale — the user sees *why* it can't be edited here rather than wondering where it went.
+**Empty State:** Add mode = blank form, Quantity on Hand shows "0 (starts at zero)."
+**Error State:** Field-level red outline + inline message, focus jumps to first invalid field on Save attempt; Save remains clickable (not blocked) per Phase 2 §6.4 — a second live-validation layer prevents most errors before Save is even pressed.
+**Success State:** Save button shows brief busy state (disabled to prevent double-submit) → dialog closes → confirmation banner on the parent list screen, new/updated row highlighted.
+**Permission Differences:** Administrator-only screen entirely — Staff never reach this dialog (no Edit icon, no Add button available to trigger it).
+**Resizing:** Fixed-size modal, not resizable (static field count per Phase 2 §2.3), centered on the main window.
+
+---
+
+## 5.6 SCR-006 / SCR-007 — Category List & Add/Edit
+
+Follows 5.3/5.5 exactly, scoped to Category, with these deltas:
+- **Grid columns:** Category ID, Name, Description, Product Count, Status, Actions.
+- **Filter:** Status (Active/Inactive) only — no stock-status filter (not applicable to categories).
+- **Add/Edit fields (flat layout, no section grouping — ≤6 fields per §3.13):** Name (required, unique, max 100), Description (optional, max 500), Active checkbox.
+- **Delete behavior:** If Product Count > 0, hard delete is blocked (BR-008) — the Blocked-Delete dialog (§6.2 in `06-Dialogs-and-States.md`) explains the count and offers "Mark Inactive" directly.
+- **Empty state:** "No categories yet. Add your first category to get started." (Admin) / "No categories match your search." + Clear Filters.
+- **Permission:** Identical Admin-full / Staff-view-only split as Product List.
+
+## 5.7 SCR-008 / SCR-009 — Supplier List & Add/Edit
+
+Deltas from the reference pattern:
+- **Grid columns:** Supplier ID, Name, Contact Person, Phone, Email, Status, Actions.
+- **Search:** Name only.
+- **Add/Edit fields (flat layout):** Name (required, max 150), Contact Person (optional, max 100), Phone (optional, format-validated — "Phone number can only contain digits, spaces, +, -, and parentheses"), Email (optional, format-validated — "Enter a valid email address"), Address (optional, max 250).
+- **Delete behavior:** Blocked if referenced by any Product or InventoryTransaction (BR-009); Blocked-Delete dialog offers "Mark Inactive."
+- **Empty state:** "No suppliers yet. Add your first supplier to get started." / "No suppliers match your search." + Clear Filters.
+- **Permission:** Same Admin/Staff split.
+
+## 5.8 SCR-010 / SCR-011 — Customer List & Add/Edit
+
+Deltas from the reference pattern:
+- **Grid columns:** Customer ID, Name, Phone, Email, Status, Actions.
+- **Search:** Name or Phone.
+- **Add/Edit fields (flat layout):** Name (required, max 150), Phone (optional, format-validated), Email (optional, format-validated), Address (optional, max 250).
+- **Delete behavior:** Blocked if referenced by any Stock-Out transaction (BR-010); Blocked-Delete dialog offers "Mark Inactive."
+- **Empty state:** "No customers yet. Add your first customer to get started." / "No customers match your search." + Clear Filters.
+- **Permission:** Same Admin/Staff split.
