+## 5.9 SCR-012 — Stock-In
+
+**Purpose:** Record goods received from a supplier.
+**Layout:** Dedicated full screen (not a modal — repeated many times per shift, per Phase 2 §5.9), single column, grouped:
+```
+Header: "Stock In"
+┌───────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│ Product & Supplier                          │
+│  Product *  [ ▾ type to search… ]  On hand: 42 │
+│  Actual Supplier * [ ▾ defaults to product's supplier ] │
+│                                              │
+│ Movement Details                             │
+│  Quantity *  [____]   → New on-hand will be: 47 (info) │
+│  Date *      [ 📅 today ]                    │
+│  Unit Price * [____]                         │
+│                                              │
+│ Notes                                        │
+│  [_____________________________] (0/500)     │
+│                                              │
+│         [Clear Form]        [Record Stock-In]│
+└───────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+**Visual Hierarchy:** Product selection (first, drives everything else) → live on-hand context next to it → quantity/date/price group → notes (lowest priority, optional) → action row.
+
+**Components:** Product ComboBox (type-to-search, active only, shows current on-hand inline), Actual Supplier ComboBox (defaults to product's default supplier, changeable per BR-028), Quantity numeric (positive integer, live "New on-hand will be: X" preview in `info` color), Date DateTimePicker (defaults today, no future dates), Unit Price numeric (≥0, 2 decimals), Notes (optional, max 500), Record Stock-In (Primary), Clear Form (Secondary).
+
+**Primary Action:** Record Stock-In.
+**Secondary Actions:** Clear Form.
+**Data Presentation:** Live inline preview values (on-hand, new-on-hand) — no confirmation dialog required for this action (Phase 2 §6.11 — Stock-In is purely additive, low-risk, and the highest-frequency task, so the live preview substitutes for a modal confirm to minimize clicks). A lightweight confirmation dialog does still appear per Phase 2 §5.9 stating "Add {qty} × {product} from {supplier}? New quantity on hand: {X}." — reconciled here as: the preview lets the user self-correct before committing, and the dialog is the final explicit confirm, consistent with both source passages.
+**Empty State:** N/A (always a blank entry form ready for input).
+**Error State:** Standard validation messaging (§3.15); Product-now-inactive edge case blocked with "This product is now inactive."; Save disabled until required fields are valid.
+**Success State:** Confirmation → form clears and refocuses the Product field for rapid repeated entry; transient status banner confirms.
+**Permission Differences:** None — both Admin and Staff have full access to this screen and action.
+**Resizing:** Single-column form stays a fixed comfortable width, centered or left-aligned within the content region; does not need to reflow narrower than 1024px minimum.
+
+---
+
+## 5.10 SCR-013 — Stock-Out
+
+**Purpose:** Record goods issued to a customer (optional).
+**Layout:** Same structural pattern as Stock-In. Groups: Product & Customer, Movement Details, Notes.
+```
+│ Product & Customer                            │
+│  Product * [ ▾ type to search… ]  Available: 42 │  ← prominent, large
+│  Customer  [ ▾ No customer selected ]  (optional, no asterisk) │
+│                                                │
+│ Movement Details                               │
+│  Quantity * [____]                              │
+│    ⚠ Insufficient stock. Available: 3.  (error, only if triggered) │
+│  Date *     [ 📅 today ]                         │
+│  Selling Price * [____]  (pre-filled, editable)  │
+```
+**Visual Hierarchy:** Available Quantity is displayed as a prominent stat directly beside the Product selector (Phase 2 explicit instruction: "Insufficient stock should be impossible to miss") → Quantity field, which turns to the error state (`borderError` 2px, red text beneath) the instant entered quantity exceeds availability, **before** Save is even attempted — this is the single most safety-critical visual behavior on this screen.
+
+**Components:** Product ComboBox (active only, "Available: {X}" stat beside selection), Customer ComboBox (optional, explicitly no red asterisk, defaults "No customer selected"), Quantity numeric (live-validated against availability), Date DateTimePicker (today default, no future), Selling Price numeric (pre-filled from product's current price, editable), Notes (optional), Record Stock-Out (Primary), Clear Form (Secondary).
+
+**Primary Action:** Record Stock-Out.
+**Secondary Actions:** Clear Form.
+**Data Presentation:** "Available: {X}" rendered as a bold inline stat, not buried in a tooltip; on insufficient-stock entry, the Quantity field's border and message switch to the Error state immediately (§3.4/§3.15).
+**Empty State:** N/A (blank entry form).
+**Error State:** "Insufficient stock. Available: {X}." inline under Quantity, red field outline, Save disabled while in this state (Phase 2 §5.10) — this is the one Stock screen where the field-level error can actively block Save before the user tries, because the risk (overselling stock) outweighs the "let them try and be told" default.
+**Success State:** Confirmation dialog ("Issue {qty} × {product} to {customer or "no customer"}? Remaining stock: {X}.") → Yes commits → transient success banner, form clears.
+**Permission Differences:** None — both Admin and Staff have full access.
+**Resizing:** Same as Stock-In.
+
+---
+
+## 5.11 SCR-014 — Inventory Adjustment (Administrator only)
+
+**Purpose:** Correct stock quantity with a mandatory reason — the highest-risk single action in the system (directly overrides stock without a supplier/customer transaction context).
+**Layout:** Single-column form, groups: Product, Quantity Correction, Reason.
+```
+Header: "Inventory Adjustment"   ← page itself only reachable/visible to Admin
+┌───────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│ Product                                     │
+│  Product * [ ▾ active products only ]        │
+│                                              │
+│ Quantity Correction                          │
+│  Previous Quantity: 42   (read-only)          │
+│  New Quantity * [____]                        │
+│  Difference: +5  (green)  /  −3 (red) / 0 (neutral) — live │
+│                                              │
+│ Reason                                       │
+│  Reason * [_______________________] (0/250)   │
+│   e.g., stock count correction, damaged goods, theft │
+│                                              │
+│                        [Save Adjustment]      │
+└───────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+**Visual Hierarchy:** This screen is deliberately given a distinct, slightly more serious visual weight than Stock-In/Out to make its administrator-only, high-risk nature obvious without inventing a new component: the Previous → New → Difference chain is laid out as an explicit visual sequence (label, arrow-like vertical flow, live-colored difference) rather than side-by-side fields, so the *size and direction of the change* is the most legible thing on the screen. Reason is a required, generously-sized text area, not an afterthought field.
+
+**Components:** Product ComboBox (active only), Previous Quantity (read-only label), New Quantity (required numeric integer ≥0), Difference (read-only, computed live, colored per sign), Reason (required multiline, max 250, explicit placeholder example text), Save Adjustment (Primary).
+
+**Primary Action:** Save Adjustment.
+**Secondary Actions:** None beyond implicit navigation away (no Clear Form — this is a deliberate, careful action, not a repeated-entry task like Stock-In).
+**Data Presentation:** Difference computed and colored live as New Quantity is typed (`success` green for positive, `error` red for negative, `textMuted` neutral for zero).
+**Empty State:** N/A (blank form).
+**Error State:** Missing Reason → Save disabled, inline "A reason is required."; standard validation otherwise.
+**Success State:** Confirmation dialog explicitly states before/after quantities and reason (the most detailed confirmation dialog in the app, matching its risk level) → Yes commits → redirect to Inventory History with the new entry visible, transient success banner.
+**Permission Differences:** This entire screen and its sidebar entry are hidden — not disabled — for Inventory/Store Staff (§3.11.1).
+**Resizing:** Single-column, fixed comfortable width, same behavior as Stock-In/Out.
+
+---
+
+## 5.12 SCR-015 — Inventory Transaction History
+
+**Purpose:** Read-only, filterable log of all stock movements — must visually communicate append-only, non-editable data.
+**Layout:**
+```
+Header: "Inventory History"
+┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│ [From 📅] [To 📅]  [Type ▾ All]  [Product ▾ type to search]  Clear Filters │
+├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
+│ ID  Date       Type      Product     Qty  Supplier/Customer  User   Notes │
+│ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────│
+│ 501 2026-08-19 ▲ Stock-In  USB-C Cable +50  ACME             J.Alvarez  — │
+│ 502 2026-08-19 ▼ Stock-Out Wireless Mouse −2  Jane Doe        M.Ochieng — │
+│ 503 2026-08-18 ● Adjustment HDMI Adapter −1  —                J.Alvarez Damaged │
+├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
+│                                                  [Print] │
+└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+**Visual Hierarchy:** Filter bar (top, always available) → grid (main content) → Print (bottom, secondary emphasis). **No Actions column at all** on this grid — its structural absence (not a disabled/greyed one) is the primary visual signal that this data is append-only (per Phase 2 §5.12: "this is the UI-level enforcement of append-only history").
+
+**Components:** Date Range (From/To DateTimePickers), Transaction Type ComboBox (All/Stock-In/Stock-Out/Adjustment), Product ComboBox (type-to-search, optional), DataGridView columns: Transaction ID, Date, Type (icon+label — up-arrow-tint for Stock-In, down-arrow-tint for Stock-Out, dot/circle-tint for Adjustment), Product, Quantity (signed, colored by direction: `success` green "+50", `error` red "−2"), Supplier/Customer (contextual to type), User, Notes; Print button.
+
+**Primary Action:** Print.
+**Secondary Actions:** Filter (live-updating).
+**Data Presentation:** Quantity column signed and colored by movement direction; Type column uses the same icon+label+color pattern as status badges for consistency, applied to transaction type rather than stock status.
+**Empty State (no data):** "No stock movements recorded yet." (§3.17).
+**Empty State (filtered, no matches):** "No transactions match your filters." + Clear Filters.
+**Error State:** ER-007/010-class friendly message, retry option.
+**Success State:** N/A directly (this screen displays the results of successful actions taken elsewhere; new rows simply appear).
+**Permission Differences:** None on this screen itself — both roles see the identical read-only grid, filters, and Print action. (The *entries* reflect whichever actions each role is permitted to take elsewhere.)
+**Resizing:** Product/Notes columns fill-weighted; ID/Date/Type/Qty fixed-width; standard vertical scroll, no pagination.
