+## 5.13 SCR-016 / SCR-017 — Reports Hub & Report Viewer
+
+**Purpose:** Select and view/print MVP reports.
+**SCR-016 Layout:**
+```
+Header: "Reports"
+┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│  [Card] Current Inventory   [Card] Low Stock    [Card] Out-of-Stock │
+│  [Card] Stock-In            [Card] Stock-Out    [Card] Transaction History │
+│   (Staff sees only: Current Inventory, Low Stock, Transaction History)     │
+├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
+│  (once a report card is selected, its filters appear here inline) │
+│  Category ▾   Stock Status ▾              [Generate]    │
+└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+**SCR-017 Layout:**
+```
+Header: "Current Inventory Report"   Filters: Category=All, Status=Low Stock
+┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│  (report table — same DataGridView visual standard,     │
+│   print-oriented: header repeats on each printed page)   │
+├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
+│                              [Back to Reports]  [Print]  │
+└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+**Visual Hierarchy:** SCR-016 — report-type Cards (§3.21) are the primary selection surface, each showing its name only until selected, then expanding its specific filter controls inline beneath. SCR-017 — the filter summary sits directly under the report title (small, `label`/`textMuted`) so a printed/viewed report is self-describing; the table itself is the dominant visual element.
+
+**Components:** SCR-016: one Card per report type available to the current role, filter ComboBoxes/DateTimePickers appearing per the selected report's definition (Category+Status for Current Inventory; Date Range+Product+Supplier for Stock-In; Date Range+Product+Customer for Stock-Out; Date Range+Type+Product for Transaction History; Low Stock and Out-of-Stock use their implicit filters with no extra controls), Generate (Primary). SCR-017: report title + filter summary, DataGridView-style report body, Print (Primary), Back to Reports (Secondary).
+
+**Primary Action:** Generate (SCR-016) / Print (SCR-017).
+**Secondary Actions:** Adjust filters and regenerate; Back (returns to SCR-016 with filters preserved, per Phase 2 §5.13).
+**Data Presentation:** Report tables reuse the exact DataGridView standard (§3.9) for visual consistency, but are styled slightly more print-friendly — header row repeats across printed pages, no row-hover/selection styling needed since it's a static, printable view rather than an interactive management grid.
+**Empty State:** "No records found for the selected filters." in the report body area.
+**Error State:** ER-007/010-class friendly message.
+**Success State:** N/A beyond the populated table itself being the successful outcome.
+**Permission Differences:** SCR-016 shows only the report Cards each role is entitled to — Administrator sees all 6; Staff see Current Inventory, Low Stock, and Transaction History only (Phase 2 §5.13) — the other three Cards are not rendered, not shown-disabled.
+**Resizing:** Report Viewer window is resizable (Phase 2 §2.3, "reports benefit from more screen space"), opens maximized or large by default — the only window in the app other than the main shell to get this treatment.
