+## 5.14 SCR-018 / SCR-019 — User Management List & Add/Edit (Administrator only)
+
+**Purpose:** Manage accounts and roles.
+**SCR-018 Layout:**
+```
+Header: "User Management"                          [+ Add User]
+┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│ [🔍 Search by name or username…]                          │
+├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
+│ Username    Full Name      Role            Status    Actions │
+│ jalvarez    Jane Alvarez   Administrator   ● Active   👁✏🗑(disabled, tooltip)│ ← current user's own row
+│ mochieng    Mercy Ochieng  Inventory Staff ● Active   👁✏🗑 │
+├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
+└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+**SCR-019 Layout:** `dialogWidthMedium` (560px), flat field list:
+```
+┌─ Add User ─────────────────────────────┐
+│  Username *  [_______________]   (disabled on Edit) │
+│  Password *  [_______________] (Create only)  │
+│  Confirm Password * [_______________] (Create only) │
+│  (Edit mode instead shows: [Reset Password] link)   │
+│  Full Name * [_______________]            │
+│  Role *      [ ▾ Administrator / Inventory Staff ]  │
+│  ☐ Active   (Edit mode)                   │
+│                          [Cancel]  [Save]  │
+└───────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+**Visual Hierarchy:** List — the current Administrator's own row visually behaves like every other row except its Deactivate icon, which renders in the standard disabled treatment (§3.1) with a tooltip, rather than being hidden — because the row itself must remain fully visible and identical in every other respect; only that one action is state-blocked. Add/Edit — Username/Role/Password fields are the highest-stakes fields on this form (account security), so they're placed first, in that priority order.
+
+**Components:** Search TextBox, DataGridView (Username, Full Name, Role, Status badge, Last Login if tracked, Actions), Username TextBox (required, unique, max 50, disabled on Edit), Password + Confirm Password (Create only, min 6 chars, masked), Reset Password ghost-link (Edit only, replaces the always-visible password field per Phase 2 §5.14/§9.5), Full Name TextBox (required), Role ComboBox (required), Active checkbox (Edit mode).
+
+**Primary Action:** "+ Add User" (list) / Save (form).
+**Secondary Actions:** Deactivate (list row, Administrator-only, self-row disabled).
+**Data Presentation:** Role rendered as plain text in the grid (not a badge — role is a fact, not a status), Status (Active/Inactive) uses the standard entity-status badge (§3.12).
+**Empty State:** Not realistically applicable (at least one Administrator account must always exist to reach this screen) — if ever empty of *other* users, no special empty-state copy is defined beyond the standard "No users match your search." for filtered/searched states.
+**Error State:** Duplicate Username ("This username is already in use."), Missing Fields (standard inline pattern).
+**Success State:** Standard Save confirmation banner + list refresh; Deactivate confirmation → "Marked Inactive," row shown greyed/Inactive-tagged.
+**Permission Differences:** This entire screen and its sidebar entry are hidden — not disabled — for Inventory/Store Staff (§3.11.1), identical treatment to Inventory Adjustment.
+**Self-Deactivation:** On the Administrator's own row, Deactivate is disabled with tooltip "You cannot deactivate your own account while logged in" (BR-020) — prevented visually rather than surfaced as a runtime permission error.
+**Resizing:** List grid standard behavior; Add/Edit dialog fixed-size modal, centered.
