+## 5.15 SCR-020 — Delegation Management (Administrator only) *(SRS v1.1)*
+
+**Purpose:** Create, view, and revoke time-bounded delegations of Stock-In, Stock-Out, or approved report access — the most visibly Administrator-exclusive screen after User Management, and the screen that must make delegation's temporary, revocable, non-role-changing nature obvious at a glance.
+
+**Layout:** List-first, matching the Inventory History anatomy rather than the master-data Add/Edit pattern — a delegation is a short-lived grant record, not a multi-field entity:
+```
+Header: "Delegation Management"                    [+ Create Delegation]
+┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│ [Recipient ▾ type to search]  [Responsibility ▾ All]  [Status ▾ All] │  Clear Filters
+├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
+│ ID  Recipient       Responsibility  Start      End        Status      Created By  Actions │
+│ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────│
+│ D-04 M. Ochieng     Stock-In        2026-08-20 2026-08-27  ✓ Active    J.Alvarez   [Revoke] │
+│ D-03 M. Ochieng     Stock-Out       2026-08-01 2026-08-10  ⏱ Expired   J.Alvarez   —        │
+│ D-02 T. Kimani      Report Access   2026-07-15 2026-07-20  ✕ Revoked   J.Alvarez   —        │
+├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
+└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+**Create Delegation panel** (modal dialog, `dialogWidthMedium` 560px, opens over the list — the underlying grid stays visible behind it, same "context isn't lost" pattern as every other Add/Edit dialog):
+```
+┌─ Create Delegation ─────────────────────┐
+│  Recipient *     [ ▾ eligible active Staff only ]  │
+│  Responsibility * [ ▾ Stock-In / Stock-Out / Report Access ] │
+│  Start Date *    [ 📅 ____ ]                       │
+│  End Date *      [ 📅 ____ ]                       │
+│  Reason *        [_______________________] (0/250) │
+│                              [Cancel]  [Save]       │
+└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+**Visual Hierarchy:** The grid's Status column is the single most important piece of information on the screen — it is the only column rendered as a badge rather than plain text, so a long delegation history remains scannable at a glance (identical priority treatment to Stock Status on Product List, §5.3). The Actions column carries **only** a "Revoke" control, and only on Active rows — Expired and Revoked rows show an em-dash in that column rather than a greyed-out button, making the read-only nature of history rows immediately legible without a tooltip. In the Create panel, Recipient and Responsibility are placed first (the two fields that define *what's being granted*), Reason last (the justification, reviewed after the grant is understood).
+
+**Components:** Recipient filter ComboBox (type-to-search, optional), Responsibility filter ComboBox (All/Stock-In/Stock-Out/Report Access), Status filter ComboBox (All/Active/Expired/Revoked), DataGridView columns: Delegation ID, Recipient, Responsibility, Start Date, End Date, Status (badge, §3.12), Created By, Actions (Revoke only, Active rows only); "+ Create Delegation" primary Button (header, top-right); Create panel: Recipient ComboBox (required, eligible active Staff only), Responsibility ComboBox (required, delegatable set only — non-delegatable items are absent from the list, §3.11.1), Start Date DateTimePicker (required), End Date DateTimePicker (required), Reason multiline TextBox (required, max 250, 0/250 counter), Cancel (secondary) / Save (primary).
+
+**Primary Action:** "+ Create Delegation" (list) / Save (panel).
+**Secondary Actions:** Revoke (list row, Active only); Filter by Recipient/Responsibility/Status.
+**Data Presentation:** Status badge is the only colored element in each row (§3.12: Active green, Expired neutral grey, Revoked red) — Start/End Date, Recipient, Responsibility, and Created By render as plain table text, keeping the badge the sole visual point of emphasis per row, consistent with how Stock Status is the sole badge on Product List.
+**Empty State:** "No delegations yet. Create one to temporarily extend a Staff member's access." + Create Delegation button (no data at all); "No delegations match your filters." + Clear Filters (filtered, no matches) — same two-tier empty-state pattern as every other list screen (§3.17).
+**Error State:** Recipient ineligible ("This user is not eligible to receive a delegation."), Responsibility not delegatable ("This responsibility cannot be delegated."), End Date before Start Date ("End date cannot be before start date."), Reason empty ("A reason is required for this delegation."), delegator lacks authority ("You cannot delegate a responsibility you do not have."), overlapping delegation ("This user already has an active delegation for this responsibility during this period.") — all inline, field-level, same visual treatment as every other validation error (§3.6/§3.16).
+**Success State:** Create → transient success banner ("Delegation created successfully"), panel closes, new row appears highlighted at the top of the grid. Revoke → confirmation dialog first (§6-equivalent, "Revoke Delegation?" / "This will immediately end {Recipient}'s access to {Responsibility}." / danger-styled "Revoke" button) → on confirm, the row updates in place to the Revoked badge, transient success banner ("Delegation revoked"), record remains visible in the grid (never removed).
+**Permission Differences:** This entire screen and its sidebar entry are hidden — not disabled — for Inventory/Store Staff, identical treatment to Inventory Adjustment and User Management (§3.11.1, UX-DEC-002). There is no reduced or read-only version of this screen for Staff — it simply does not exist in their build of the shell.
+**Resizing:** List grid uses the standard DataGridView resizing rules (§3.9) — Recipient/Reason-adjacent columns fill-weighted, ID/Date/Status/Actions fixed-width; Create panel is a fixed-size modal, centered, identical sizing behavior to every other master-data Add/Edit dialog.
+
+---
+
+## 5.16 Cross-Screen Consistency Check
+
+Every screen above reuses, without deviation: the same header pattern (§3.22/§4.2), the same list-screen anatomy (search/filter bar → grid → footer), the same Add/Edit anatomy (grouped fields → Cancel/Save footer), the same status-badge component (§3.12) wherever status appears, the same confirmation-dialog pattern (`06-Dialogs-and-States.md`) wherever a destructive or high-risk action occurs, and the same empty/error/success visual language throughout. No screen introduces a one-off component, color, or layout idiom not defined in `02-Design-Tokens.md` or `03-Component-Library.md`. **SCR-020 (Delegation Management, SRS v1.1) is held to the identical standard:** its list follows the Inventory History anatomy exactly (filter bar → grid → no Edit action, §5.12), its Create panel follows the standard Add/Edit dialog anatomy exactly (§5.5), and its status badge reuses existing color tokens rather than introducing new ones (§3.12) — it was designed as an extension of the existing language, not a new one.
